# Line endings, for the two kinds of file where they change behaviour.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is on for this checkout, so git rewrites LF to CRLF on
# the way out. That is harmless for most files and not for these two.
#
# `.mjs` — the scripts start with `#!/usr/bin/env node`. Vite strips a shebang
# before evaluating a module, and with CRLF it stops matching: the line survives
# into the transformed output and every test that imports one of these dies with
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`. It cost four test files on launch
# day, and it appeared at a checkout rather than at an edit, which is what made
# it confusing — nothing in the diff explained it.
#
# `.sql` — `supabase/seed/catalog.sql` is generated and committed, and a test
# compares the committed bytes against a freshly generated copy. The generator
# writes LF. If git hands the test CRLF, the comparison fails for a reason that
# has nothing to do with the catalogue.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
